weave-knee trial v1
fanout: 10
seed: 1
weaver: claude-sonnet-5
judge: claude-sonnet-5
quality: 3
narrative:
  Toldor forms a closed ring of ten modules, each handing its work to the next until the circuit returns to where it began. At the head sits Zinhul, the gate, which evicts anything left unclaimed after 10 ticks, retries a failed handoff at most 1 time before parking it, and acts only once 4 of its peers countersign. Zinhul hands its sealed ledger to Grihul, the warden, and the ring closes on the other side when Ruvfel reports missed heartbeats to Zinhul.

  Grihul retries a failed handoff at most 2 times before parking it, keeps only digests of what it carries and never the bodies, and acts only once 2 of its peers countersign. Having received Zinhul's sealed ledger, Grihul signals backpressure onward to Nexquen, the relay.

  Nexquen refuses new writes while its sweep is running, answers reads from its newest snapshot only, and retries a failed handoff at most 4 times before parking it. Taking in Grihul's backpressure signal, Nexquen delegates its overflow to Tolzin, the cache.

  Tolzin answers reads from its newest snapshot only, keeps digests of what it carries and never the bodies, and refuses new writes while its sweep is running. Receiving Nexquen's overflow, Tolzin reports missed heartbeats to Felpam, the broker.

  Felpam evicts anything left unclaimed after 10 ticks, acts only once 2 of its peers countersign, and refuses new writes while its sweep is running. Having received Tolzin's heartbeat reports, Felpam streams its evictions to Osthul, the monitor.

  Osthul answers reads from its newest snapshot only, evicts anything left unclaimed after 9 ticks, and acts only once 4 of its peers countersign. Taking in Felpam's stream of evictions, Osthul publishes its sweep verdicts to Zingri, the sampler.

  Zingri acts only once 2 of its peers countersign, refuses new writes while its sweep is running, and evicts anything left unclaimed after 11 ticks. Receiving Osthul's sweep verdicts, Zingri hands its sealed ledger to Nexkel, the index.

  Nexkel answers reads from its newest snapshot only, retries a failed handoff at most 4 times before parking it, and evicts anything left unclaimed after 12 ticks. Having received Zingri's sealed ledger, Nexkel signals backpressure to Hulost, the beacon.

  Hulost evicts anything left unclaimed after 6 ticks, keeps digests of what it carries and never the bodies, and retries a failed handoff at most 3 times before parking it. Taking in Nexkel's backpressure signal, Hulost delegates its overflow to Ruvfel, the courier.

  Ruvfel evicts anything left unclaimed after 6 ticks, keeps digests of what it carries and never the bodies, and answers reads from its newest snapshot only. Receiving Hulost's overflow, Ruvfel reports missed heartbeats back to Zinhul, closing the ring that opened this account.
